{"id":"u-4956883c-ed5d-45b4-94e8-28b62b8e88ac","src":"community","title":"Gym Geek’s 5 Day PPLUL Split - J. Litfin","author":"M.A.D.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/gym-geek-s-5-day-pplul-split-j-litfin","desc":"This increase in frequency and volume is the key advantage of PPLUL over bro splits, since it promotes greater muscle hypertrophy and uses your training time more efficiently.\n\nTips for the PPLUL split\n\nCardio:\nIt’s a good idea to add some cardio alongside your PPLUL split workout routine. Cardio enhances your overall fitness and can increase your endurance. Here are some ways you could include cardio into your routine:\n\n* Cardio on rest days: This is a practical option that separates cardio from your strength training. Try to engage in light to moderate cardio like jogging or cycling on these days.\n\n* Post-workout cardio: After completing your strength training, incorporate a short, high-intensity cardio session. This burns calories efficiently without draining your energy for lifting.\n\nRest between sets\nAllow 2-3 minutes of rest between sets for your muscles to recover and to prevent injuries.\nWhen lifting heavier weights with a lower rep range, you will need a longer rest period than with high-rep, low weight exercises. Compound exercises typically need a longer rest period than isolation exercises.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":11,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-15T02:29:19.280Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push","Pull","Legs","Rest","Upper Body","Lower Body","Rest"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Cable Crossover","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Shoulder Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Assisted